  "presentation_summary": [
    "69-year-old Asian man presented in August 2018 with five days of subjective fever, chills, and generalized weakness after a golfing trip in Westchester, New York.",
    "Emergency-department vitals showed temperature 39.7 degC, heart rate 77-122/min, respiratory rate 15-26/min, and blood pressure 85/39 to 118/69 mmHg responsive to 3 liters of normal saline.",
    "Exam showed mild yellow conjunctival tint. Labs showed hemoglobin 8.7 g/dL, hematocrit 26.4%, WBC 4.71 x10^9/L, platelets 37 x10^9/L, haptoglobin <10 mg/dL, total bilirubin 3.5 mg/dL, direct bilirubin 1.6 mg/dL, indirect bilirubin 1.9 mg/dL, LDH 636 U/L, BUN 29 mg/dL, creatinine 1.39 mg/dL, and sodium 131 mmol/L.",
    "Blood smear showed no schistocytes but possible parasites in RBCs; imaging showed mild splenomegaly. Three blood cultures had no bacterial growth.",
    "Babesia DNA real-time PCR was positive; Lyme and Anaplasma testing were negative. Hemoglobin and platelets improved with clindamycin, quinine, and doxycycline."
  ],
